e>14</volume><fpage>305</fpage><lpage>308</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Mahan J, Selgison D, Henry SL et al (1991) Factors in pin tract infections. Orthopaedics 14:305&#x02013;308 </citation></ref><ref id="CR9"><label>9.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Termaat</surname><given-names>M.F.</given-names></name><name><surname>Raijmakers</surname><given-names>P.G.</given-names></name><name><surname>Scholten</surname><given-names>H.J.</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><article-title>The accuracy of diagnostic imaging for the assessment of chronic osteomyelitis: a systematic review and meta-analysis</article-title><source>J Bone Joint Surg Am</source><year>2005</year><volume>87</volume><fpage>2464</fpage><lpage>2471</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.2106/JBJS.D.02691</pub-id></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Termaat MF, Raijmakers PG, Scholten HJ et al (2005) The accuracy of diagnostic imaging for the assessment of chronic osteomyelitis: a systematic review and meta-analysis. J Bone Joint Surg Am 87:2464&#x02013;2471 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16264122</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="CR10"><label>10.</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hughes</surname><given-names>D.K.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Nuclear medicine and infection detection: the relative effectiveness of imaging with 111 In-Oxine-, 99mTc-HMPAO-, and 99mTc-stannous fluoride colloid-labeled leukocytes and with 67 Ga-citrate</article-title><source>J Nucl Med Technol</source><year>2003</year><volume>31</volume><fpage>196</fpage><lpage>201</lpage></citation><citation citation-type="display-unstructured">Hughes DK (2003) Nuclear medicine and infection detection: the relative effectiveness of imaging with 111 In-Oxine-, 99mTc-HMPAO-, and 99mTc-stannous fluoride colloid-labeled leukocytes and with 67 Ga-citrate. J Nucl Med Technol 31:196&#x02013;201 <pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">14657285</pub-id></citation></ref></ref-list></back></article>